          "short": "$\\frac{1}{36}$\n\nDivide before subtracting, then use a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\div3&=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{1}{3}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\div3&=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{9}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\div3&=\\frac{9}{36}-\\frac{8}{36}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\div3&=\\frac{1}{36}\\end{aligned}$$",
